# MSA Schedule 4 — Chronic failure

> Module ChronicFailure

L-6.1 gives the Customer a termination right on a **pattern** of failures
rather than on any single one, and the pattern has two independent triggers:
three consecutive Measurement Periods below 99.90%, or any four Measurement
Periods in a rolling twelve-month period. Either suffices, so a history can
satisfy the second without ever satisfying the first. L-6.2 then puts a 30-day
exercise window on the right, running from the end of the Measurement Period
which gives rise to it, and lapses it per occurrence. That window has two ends
and each occurrence has its own, so this scope identifies the occurrence it is
assessing before it computes any deadline at all.

The history is a list of Measurement Periods. Because L-2.1 makes a
Measurement Period a calendar month, each period is identified by the first
day of its month, which makes "consecutive" and "rolling twelve months" exact
month arithmetic rather than an approximation in days — and adding a month to
the first day of a month is never ambiguous, so no rounding mode is needed.
The availability figure on each period is the L-2.3 figure, already rounded to
two decimal places.

There are no judgement inputs. Every term is arithmetic over the history, a
date of record, or the fact of whether notice was given.

## Prologue — declarations

```catala-metadata
declaration structure PeriodAvailability:
  # L-2.1: the calendar month, identified by its first and last day.
  data period_start content date
  data period_end content date
  # L-2.3: the Availability Percentage, rounded to two decimal places, on the
  # 0-100 scale.
  data availability_percentage content decimal

declaration scope ChronicFailureRight:
  input availability_history content list of PeriodAvailability
  input assessment_date content date
  input notice_given content boolean
  input notice_date content date
  output failing_periods content list of PeriodAvailability
  output consecutive_trigger content boolean
  output rolling_trigger content boolean
  output right_arisen content boolean
  output completing_periods content list of PeriodAvailability
  # L-6.2 confines a lapse to "that occurrence", so the occurrence being
  # assessed has to be identified before any deadline is computed: those that
  # have arisen by the assessment date, those of them whose window is still
  # open, and the one the assessment actually rests on.
  output arisen_occurrences content list of PeriodAvailability
  output live_occurrences content list of PeriodAvailability
  output assessed_occurrences content list of PeriodAvailability
  output trigger_period_end content optional of date
  output notice_period_days content integer
  output early_termination_charges_payable content boolean
  output exercise_deadline content optional of date
  # Whether the notice of record falls inside both ends of the L-6.2 window.
  output notice_exercises_the_right content boolean
  output right_lapsed content boolean
  output right_exercisable content boolean
```

## L-6.1 The two triggers

| MSA-SCH4 L-6.1 (004-msa-sla-credits.md:102)
|
| Where the Availability Percentage is less than 99.90% in each of three
| consecutive Measurement Periods, or in any four Measurement Periods in a rolling
| twelve-month period, the Customer may terminate the Agreement in respect of the
| affected Service on 30 days' written notice, without liability for early
| termination charges.

"Less than 99.90%" is strict on both triggers, matching L-3.1: a period at
exactly 99.90% is not a failing period and breaks a run.

Both triggers are expressed as tests on a single **completing** period — the
period at whose end the pattern is complete. That is the period L-6.2 calls
"the Measurement Period which gives rise to it", so computing the triggers
this way yields the exercise window as well as the right.

  * consecutive: the period fails, and so do the two calendar months
    immediately before it. Three is the stated number, so two consecutive
    failures are not enough and a gap of one good month resets the run.
  * rolling: the period fails, and counting back across the twelve months
    ending with it there are at least four failing periods. Four is the stated
    number, and eleven months back from the completing month is the first
    month of the twelve-month window.

The two are independent disjuncts, not exceptions to one another, so
`right_arisen` is a disjunction. The remaining limbs of L-6.1 — 30 days'
written notice and no liability for early termination charges — are stated
constants.

```catala
scope ChronicFailureRight:
  definition failing_periods equals
    list of p among availability_history such that
      p.availability_percentage < 99.90

  definition consecutive_trigger equals
    number of (list of p among failing_periods such that
      ((exists q among failing_periods such that
          q.period_start = p.period_start - 1 month)
       and (exists r among failing_periods such that
          r.period_start = p.period_start - 2 month))) > 0

  definition rolling_trigger equals
    number of (list of p among failing_periods such that
      (number of (list of q among failing_periods such that
         ((q.period_start <= p.period_start)
          and (q.period_start >= p.period_start - 11 month)))) >= 4) > 0

  definition right_arisen equals consecutive_trigger or rolling_trigger

  definition completing_periods equals
    list of p among failing_periods such that
      (((exists q among failing_periods such that
           q.period_start = p.period_start - 1 month)
        and (exists r among failing_periods such that
           r.period_start = p.period_start - 2 month))
       or (number of (list of q among failing_periods such that
             ((q.period_start <= p.period_start)
              and (q.period_start >= p.period_start - 11 month)))) >= 4)

  definition notice_period_days equals 30

  definition early_termination_charges_payable equals false
```

## L-6.2 Which occurrence is assessed

| MSA-SCH4 L-6.2 (004-msa-sla-credits.md:108)
|
| The right in L-6.1 must be exercised within 30 days after the end of the
| Measurement Period which gives rise to it, failing which it lapses in respect of
| that occurrence.

"The Measurement Period which gives rise to it" is a completing period. A
history can contain more than one, and the closing words of L-6.2 confine the
lapse to "that occurrence" — the occurrence whose own window expired — and so
expressly preserve every later one.

An earlier version took `trigger_period_end` as the **minimum** period end
over all completing periods, so the whole scope answered about the earliest
occurrence ever recorded. A cluster of failures in early 2024 whose window
closed on 30 April 2024 therefore destroyed the right arising from a fresh
cluster in 2025, and notice served five days after that 2025 occurrence arose
was reported out of time by fifteen months. Found by the adversarial
reviewer; see tests/counterexamples/CE-0007.yaml.

The occurrence assessed is the one live at the assessment date. An occurrence
arises only when its completing period ends, so `arisen_occurrences` drops
completing periods ending after the assessment date, and `live_occurrences`
keeps those of them whose 30-day window has not closed. The latest live
occurrence governs, being the one with a window still to run; failing that
the latest occurrence to have arisen, so a lapse is reported against the
occurrence it belongs to; failing that the latest completing period, so that
no deadline is manufactured for a right that has not yet arisen.
`completing_periods` stays an output, so every occurrence remains visible.

```catala
scope ChronicFailureRight:
  definition arisen_occurrences equals
    list of p among completing_periods such that
      p.period_end <= assessment_date

  definition live_occurrences equals
    list of p among arisen_occurrences such that
      (p.period_end + 30 day) >= assessment_date

  definition assessed_occurrences equals
    if (number of live_occurrences) > 0 then live_occurrences
    else if (number of arisen_occurrences) > 0 then arisen_occurrences
    else completing_periods

  definition trigger_period_end equals
    if right_arisen then
      Present content
        (maximum of (map each p among assessed_occurrences to p.period_end)
         or if list empty then assessment_date)
    else Absent

  definition exercise_deadline equals
    match trigger_period_end with pattern
    -- Absent: Absent
    -- Present content d: Present content (d + 30 day)
```

## L-6.2 Exercise inside the window, and lapse

| MSA-SCH4 L-6.2 (004-msa-sla-credits.md:108)
|
| The right in L-6.1 must be exercised within 30 days after the end of the
| Measurement Period which gives rise to it, failing which it lapses in respect of
| that occurrence.

L-6.2 fixes a window with two ends, not just a deadline. The right "must be
exercised within 30 days after the end of the Measurement Period which gives
rise to it": the window opens when that period ends, because L-6.1 confers the
right only on the expiry of the third failing period, and closes on the
thirtieth day after it. "Within 30 days" is inclusive of the thirtieth, as in
L-5.1, so the window is days 1 to 30 after the end of that period.

An earlier version tested only the upper bound — `if notice_given then
notice_date > deadline else assessment_date > deadline` — so any notice
bearing a date on or before the deadline was treated as a good exercise,
including one dated before the third failing period had even ended, and the
right was then reported as exercisable indefinitely. A notice cannot exercise
a right that did not exist when it was served. Found by the adversarial
reviewer; see tests/counterexamples/CE-0008.yaml.

So `notice_exercises_the_right` requires the notice to fall inside both ends
of the window, and the right lapses where no such exercise occurred and the
window has since closed, measured against the assessment date. The exception
repeats the parent's condition `right_arisen`, since a right that never arose
cannot lapse — a Catala exception does not inherit its parent's condition,
and the base case here is the unconditional "has not lapsed".

```catala
scope ChronicFailureRight:
  definition notice_exercises_the_right equals
    notice_given
    and (match trigger_period_end with pattern
         -- Absent: false
         -- Present content t: notice_date > t)
    and (match exercise_deadline with pattern
         -- Absent: false
         -- Present content d: notice_date <= d)

  label l6_2_not_lapsed definition right_lapsed equals false

  label l6_2_lapsed exception l6_2_not_lapsed definition right_lapsed
    under condition
      right_arisen
      and (not notice_exercises_the_right)
      and (match exercise_deadline with pattern
           -- Absent: false
           -- Present content d: assessment_date > d)
    consequence equals true

  definition right_exercisable equals right_arisen and (not right_lapsed)
```
